{
  "_what": "Metadata harvest of the 29 GRIGOLETTO template files that the geometry harvest could not reach, taken 2026-08-01 from the Figma REST endpoints that are NOT on the exhausted budget.",
  "_the_budget_model_was_wrong_and_this_corrects_it": "The recorded understanding was that the whole REST API is spent against the file OWNER's plan budget until ~4 August. MEASURED 2026-08-01: the budget is per ENDPOINT CLASS, and only the document-TREE class is spent. /v1/files/:key and /v1/files/:key/nodes return 429 with Retry-After ~324000s (3.7 days, the owner budget). /meta, /versions, /components, /styles, /images (render) and /files/:key/images (fills) all return 200 today, subject only to a SHORT rate limit whose Retry-After is single-digit seconds and which a backoff clears. The first pass through this harvest read one 429 and concluded the whole API was shut; six of seven classes were open.",
  "_what_is_still_blocked": "Auto-layout geometry (itemSpacing, padding*) lives in the document tree, so the 8-point conformance measurement that blueprint-vs-pack.json holds for 9 templates cannot be extended to these 29 until either the tree budget refills (~4-5 August) or the files are duplicated into an account we own, at which point the owner is us.",
  "_the_finding": "EVERY ONE of the 29 files is named `Daily Hero N -  Arkkhe` and authored by the same handle, while the pack lists them under invented product names (Aero Sync, Coda Noir, Bluebird...). The marketing names correspond to nothing in the files. 29 of 29 listed names do not appear in their file's real name. A reader treating the pack as 39 distinct template products is reading the packaging, not the artefacts.",
  "measured_at": "2026-08-01",
  "source_endpoints": [
    "/v1/files/:key/meta",
    "/v1/files/:key/versions"
  ],
